Below is a goal model decomposition for the described multi-robot mission. This includes both goals and tasks structured in a hierarchical tree format, with logical relationships detailed.

### Goals Table

| Name         | Text                                                                                   | Runtime          | Goal Type | Relation   |
|--------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------|-----------|------------|
| G1: Mission  | Complete the resource collection and delivery mission                                   | -                | Achieve   | AND        |
| G2: Collection | Collect specified resources from storage                                              | PARALLEL         | Perform   | AND        |
| G3: Resource Retrieval | Retrieve specific resources from storage when requested                                 | -                | Perform   | AND        |
| G4: Delivery | Deliver collected resources to the specified location                                   | PARALLEL         | Perform   | AND        |
| G5: Battery Management | Manage low battery situations during missions                                          | PARALLEL         | Achieve   | AND        |
| G6: Resource Handling on Failure | Handle resource return in case of low battery or mission failure                       | FALLBACK(G7, G8) | Achieve   | AND        |
| G7: Return to Checkpoint | Return resources to checkpoint upon low battery in delivery phase                        | -                | Perform   | -          |
| G8: Trigger Alert | Trigger alert and report to sector manager if unable to return resource                 | -                | Perform   | -          |

### Tasks Table

| Name        | Text                                                                                         | Relation   | Location      | Number of Robots |
|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|---------------|------------------|
| AT1: Go to Storage | Navigate robot to storage location to collect resources                                  | AND        | Storage       | 1                |
| AT2: Send Request | Send message to storage specifying required resources                                      | AND        | Storage       | 1                |
| AT3: Retrieve Resources | Wait and retrieve resources from storage                                                  | AND        | Storage       | 1                |
| AT4: Deliver Resources | Transport resources to the specified destination                                         | AND        | Destination   | 1                |
| AT5: Monitor Battery | Continuously monitor robot battery levels                                                 | AND        | N/A           | 1                |
| AT6: Return to Recharge | Return robot to recharge station upon low battery during collection                         | AND        | Recharge Station | 1                |
| AT7: Assign Mission | Assign mission to another robot if the current one returns for recharging                   | AND        | N/A           | 1                |
| AT8: Return to Checkpoint | Return resources to checkpoint if battery is low during delivery                          | AND        | Checkpoint    | 1                |
| AT9: Trigger Alert | Trigger alert and report failure to return resources to sector manager                       | AND        | N/A           | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G4, G5 [AND][PARALLEL]**  
  - Collect resources, deliver them, and manage battery situations must all be addressed.
  
- **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**  
  - Navigating to storage, sending the request, and retrieving resources are sequential actions for collection.

- **G4 -> AT4, G5 [AND][PARALLEL]**  
  - Delivering resources and monitoring battery run in parallel to ensure timely delivery and battery management.

- **G5 -> AT5, G6 [AND][PARALLEL]**  
  - Battery must be monitored continuously, with contingency plans for low-battery situations.

- **G6 -> G7, G8 [AND][FALLBACK]**  
  - If the battery is low during delivery, either return resources to a checkpoint or trigger an alert.

This goal model captures all necessary aspects of the mission, ensuring both resource handling and robot management are addressed.
